// src/gen/gen.zen
// Code generation: the end of the pipeline.
//
// This file is the module's public surface only — a folder root is a
// file of starred re-exports. A name absent here is module-private.
//
// THE SPLIT (STYLE.md's own example of splitting by subject): `gen` is
// BACKEND-SHARED PLUMBING, `gen_c` is THE C BACKEND. Shared: where bytes
// go and in what order (`gen_emit`), what a name is in a flat target
// namespace (`gen_name`), what a backend says when it can't lower
// something (`gen_diag`). Nothing that knows C struct layout lives
// outside `gen_c`. PLAN.md says no second backend is planned, but the
// seam costs nothing to keep honest and is cheap insurance regardless.
//
// DETERMINISM IS DESIGNED IN, NOT CHECKED FOR: same input, byte-identical
// output across runs, processes, absolute roots, input order. Three
// mechanisms:
//   - `Emit` is the only way a byte leaves this folder; `order` is the
//     only way a collection gets ordered. Nothing iterates a `Map`.
//   - A symbol name is `tcode`, a pure function of the TYPE — never a
//     counter, never which module asked first.
//   - `Span` carries a file relative to the compilation root, so two
//     checkouts of one tree emit the same bytes.
//
// THE ONLY `Err` IS `AllocError`. A form the backend can't lower becomes
// a `Diag` collected in a `Vec` (as sema does): a half-understood program
// still emits the C it could, and the caller decides whether that's a
// translation unit or a report.

// where the bytes go, and the one ordering primitive
Emit*, order*, INDENT*                   = gen.gen_emit

// what a name is when the target has one flat namespace
USR*, GEN*, RES_PATH*                    = gen.gen_name
comp*, count*, path*, path_with*, segments* = gen.gen_name
sym_type*, sym_fn*, sym_variant*         = gen.gen_name
sym_member*, sym_local*, sym_value*, sym_gen* = gen.gen_name
tcode*, module_of*, res_arity*, is_failure*   = gen.gen_name

// what a backend says when it cannot lower something
GenFault*, GenDiag*, render_gen*         = gen.gen_diag
message*, detail*                        = gen.gen_diag

// THE C BACKEND
CBackend*, emit_program*, Dest*          = gen.gen_c
ctype*, C_STANDARD*, emit_types*         = gen.gen_c
